of "depth" NHack had. It was just hack'n'slash and because it had only one
author (I think) it was just a big world without much content. There were
some great ideas in it too because I kept playing it for a few months, but
I just can't remember them anymore. :)

I also didn't like that the dungeons were so big that they didn't fit the
80x25 screen and scrolling just didn't feel appropriate.

